For each $z$ we calculate the corresponding second moment contribution to be
	\[
	\mathbb{E}_{n,n\alpha}[Z^2[z]]
	= 2^n \binom{n}{nz}
	\bigg( 1 - \frac{2}{2^k} + \bigg(\frac{z}{2}\bigg)^k \bigg)^{n\alpha}
	= \frac{\exp\{ n
	\textup{\textsf{f}}_{\textsc{sat},2}(z;\alpha) \}}
	{ n^{O(1)}}\,,\]
where the exponent $\textup{\textsf{f}}_{\textsc{sat},2}(z;\alpha)$
can be derived using Stirling's formula,
and does not depend on $n$:
	\begin{equation}\label{e:basic.second.moment.z}
	\textup{\textsf{f}}_{\textsc{sat},2}(z;\alpha)\equiv
	\underbrace{
	\bigg[\ln2 + \mathcal{H}(z)
	\bigg]
	}_{\text{entropy term}}
	+
	\underbrace{\alpha\ln\bigg( 1 - \frac{2}{2^k}
		+ \bigg(\frac{z}{2}\bigg)^k 
		 \bigg)}
		_{\text{probability term}}
	\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{H}(z)=-z\ln z-(1-z)\ln(1-z)$ denotes the standard entropy function.

It follows that
for all $\mathscr{D}'$ sufficiently close to $\mathscr{D}_\star$ we have
	\begin{equation}\label{e:compare.second.mmt.around.DDtyp}
	\mathbb{E}_{n,n\alpha}(Z\,|\,\mathscr{D}')\ll
	\sum_{\mathscr{D}}
		\mathbb{P}_{n,n\alpha}(\mathscr{D})
		\,\mathbb{E}_{n,n\alpha}(Z\,|\,\mathscr{D})
	=\mathbb{E}_{n,n\alpha} Z\,.
	\end{equation}

