		has type $(\bm{L},j)$})
	\\
	(\omega_{\bm{L},j}
	: \textup{some edge in $\delta\mathscr{U}$
		has type $(\bm{L},j)$})\\
	(\omega_{\bm{L},j}
	: \textup{some edge in $E \setminus E_{\mathscr{U}}$
		has type $(\bm{L},j)$})
	\end{pmatrix}\,.
	\]
We also abbreviate
$\omega_U
\equiv(\omega_\textup{in},\omega_{\delta U})$ and
$\omega_\textup{bd}\equiv(\omega_{\delta U},\omega_\textup{out})$. Assume the neighborhood profile $\mathscr{D}$ of $\mathscr{G}$
is bounded away from zero in the sense of \eqref{e:pos.frac}. Then, using the notation of Definition~\ref{d:judicious.augmented.alphabet}, we have
\begin{align*}
	&\max_{\acute{\omega}}
