Thus $(\eta^\ell)_{\ell\ge0}$ is a Cauchy sequence in $L^p$, hence it must converge in $L^p$ to a limiting random variable $\eta$ as $\ell\to\infty$. It follows that $\mu^\ell$ converges weakly to a limiting probability measure $\mu$ as $\ell\to\infty$. Since $\mu^\ell = \bm{R}\mu^{\ell-1}$ and the mapping $\bm{R}$ is continuous with respect to the weak topology on the space of distributions, we conclude $\mu = \bm{R}\mu$.

