		\prod_{z\in\partial a \setminus \set{u,w}} h_{za}
	\bigg]\,,
	\]

We can sample from ${\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}_\epsilon$ in the following way: first sample $\mathscr{T}\sim{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}$. Declare each clause of $\mathscr{T}$ to be ``open'' with probability $\epsilon$, independently over all clauses. For each open clause $a$, choose one of its child variables $u\in\partial a$ uniformly at random, and declare $u$ to be ``open'' as well. Let $V'$ be the (random) set of all open variables in $B_R(v_\textup{\textsc{rt}};\mathscr{T})$, and let $\mathscr{T}'$ be the connected component of $\mathscr{T}\setminus V'$ that contains $v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}$ --- as a shorthand we will write $\mathscr{T}'\equiv \mathscr{T}'(V')$. Then $\mathscr{T}'$ is a sample from ${\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}_\epsilon$. Let $\gamma_\epsilon(\cdot\,|\,\mathscr{T})$ denote the law of $V'$ given $\mathscr{T}$. 
Let $\Omega'$ denote the subspace of $\mathscr{T}$ for which 
$|B_R(v_\textup{\textsc{rt}};\mathscr{T})| \le M'$, where $M'$ will be chosen below. Then
	\begin{align*}
	P(\epsilon)&\equiv {\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}_\epsilon\Big(\textup{$v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}$
		is not stable}\Big)
	\ge
	\int_{\Omega'} \int
	\mathbf{1}\Big\{
	\textup{$v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}$ not stable in $\mathscr{T}'(V')$}
	\Big\}
	\,d\gamma_\epsilon(V'\,|\,\mathscr{T})
	\,d{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(\mathscr{T})\\
	&\ge\int_{\Omega'}
	\sum_{u \in B_R(v_\textup{\textsc{rt}};\mathscr{T}) \setminus v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}}
	\mathbf{1}\Big\{
	\textup{$v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}$ not stable in $\mathscr{T}'(\set{u})$}
	\Big\}
	\int
	\mathbf{1}\Big\{V' = \set{u}
	\Big\}\,d\gamma_\epsilon(V'\,|\,\mathscr{T})
	\,d{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(\mathscr{T})\\
	&\ge 
	\frac{\epsilon(1-\epsilon)^{M'}}{M'}
	\int_{\Omega'}
	\sum_{u \in B_R(v_\textup{\textsc{rt}};\mathscr{T}) \setminus v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}}
	\mathbf{1}\Big\{
	\textup{$v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}$ not stable in $\mathscr{T}'(\set{u})$}
	\Big\}\,d{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(\mathscr{T})\,,
	\end{align*}
where, for any $\mathscr{T}\in\Omega'$ and any $u\in B_R(v_\textup{\textsc{rt}};\mathscr{T})\setminus\set{v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}}$, the quantity $\epsilon(1-\epsilon)^{M'}/M'$ a crude lower bound on the chance that $V'=\set{u}$. If we rearrange the above and consider the contribution outside $\Omega'$, we obtain
	\begin{align*}
	P' &\equiv \int
	\sum_{u \in B_R(v_\textup{\textsc{rt}};\mathscr{T}) \setminus v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}}
	\mathbf{1}\Big\{
	\textup{$v_\textup{\textsc{rt}}$ not stable in $\mathscr{T}'(\set{u})$}
	\Big\}\,d{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(\mathscr{T})\\
	&\le\frac{P(\epsilon) M'}{\epsilon(1-\epsilon)^{M'}}
	+ \mathbb{E}\bigg[\Big|B_R(v_\textup{\textsc{rt}};\mathscr{T})\Big| 
		; \Big|B_R(v_\textup{\textsc{rt}};\mathscr{T})\Big| \ge M'\bigg]
	\le
	\frac1{\exp(\Omega(2^{k/12}R))}
	\,,
	\end{align*}
where the last bound follows by 
taking $M'=1/\epsilon = \exp(k^2R)$, and applying
Lemma~\ref{l:martingale.bound.PGW} with Lemma~\ref{l:root.is.stable.EPSILON}.
Combining the above with the $\epsilon=0$ case of 
Lemma~\ref{l:root.is.stable.EPSILON} gives
