First we use Lemma~\ref{l:radon.derivative.pgwT}
to transfer the 
result of Corollary~\ref{c:excellent}
(from \S\ref{ss:orderly.contained}) from the ${\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}$ measure to the ${\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(T)$ measure of Definition~\ref{d:PGW.based.on.T}, where $T$ is any fixed sparse tree:

\label{l:PGW.bound.on.corrupt.tree}
Let $\mathfrak{c}$ be an absolute constant. For $\mathscr{T}\sim{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}$ let $A(\mathscr{T})$ denote the set of all variables in $\mathscr{T}$ that are improper or not $\mathfrak{i}$-excellent. It holds for all $s\ge 100R$ that
	\[
	{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}\bigg(
	\begin{array}{c}
	\textup{some $T\in\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathfrak{c},s}$ is $1/(80R)$-corrupt}\\
	\textup{with respect to $(\mathscr{T},A(\mathscr{T}))$}
	\end{array}
	\bigg)
	\le \frac1{\exp(2^{k\delta_*/4} s/k^2)}\]
provided $k\ge k_0$, where $k_0$ is an absolute constant
depending only on $\delta_*$ and $\mathfrak{c}$.

\begin{proof}
This argument is similar to (but simpler than) part of the proof of Lemma~\ref{lem-local-D-0}.
First we fix a tree $T'\in\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathfrak{c},s}$, as well as a subset $B'\subseteq V_T$
with $|B'| \ge |V_T|/(80R)$ such that all variables in $B'$ lie at pairwise distance greater than $2R$.
For this fixed pair $(T',B')$ we bound (cf.\ \eqref{e:expected.number.of.embeddings}, \eqref{e:embeddings.times.embedded.probab}, and \eqref{e:product.over.disjoint.nbhds.around.sparse.tree})
	\begin{align*}
	P(T',B')
	&\equiv{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}\bigg(
	\textup{there exists an embedding $\zeta:T'\hookrightarrow\mathscr{T}$
	such that $\zeta(B')\subseteq A(\mathscr{T})$}\bigg) \\
	&\le\int\bigg|\bigg\{
	\textup{embeddings $\zeta:T'\hookrightarrow\mathscr{T}$
		such that $\zeta(B')\subseteq A(\mathscr{T})$}
	\bigg\}\bigg|\,d{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(\mathscr{T})\\
	&= \textup{\textsf{emb}}(T')
	\cdot \Big[{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(T')\Big]\bigg( B'\subseteq A(\mathscr{T}) \bigg)
	\le (\alpha k^2)^{\mathfrak{c} s}\cdot
	\prod_{u\in B'}\bigg\{
	\Big[{\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(T_u)\Big]\bigg( \textup{root of $\mathscr{T}'$ 
		is in $A(\mathscr{T}')$} \bigg)\bigg\}\,,
	\end{align*}
where $T_u$ now refers to the tree $T'$ rerooted at $u$, $\mathscr{T}'$ refers to a sample from the measure ${\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(T_u)$, and the probability factorizes over $u\in B'$ since ``proper'' and ``$\mathfrak{i}$-excellent''
are properties of the $R$-neighborhood, and we have assumed that variables in $B'$ lie at pairwise distance greater than $2R$. Applying Corollary~\ref{c:excellent.under.uPGW.T} (for the measures ${\textup{\textbf{PGW}}}(T_u)$) and summing over all possibilities of $(T',B')$ gives
	\[\sum_{T',B'}P(T',B')
	\le \frac{e^{O(\mathfrak{c} k s)}}{ \exp(2^{k\delta_*/4} s / (80k) ) }
	\le \frac1{ \exp(2^{k\delta_*/4} s/k^2) }\,.\]
This implies the assertion of the lemma.
\end{proof}

