 \label{l:corrupt.tree.in.erdos.renyi}
Let $\mathfrak{c}$ be an absolute constant. For $\mathscr{G}=(V,F,E)\sim\mathbb{P}\equiv\mathbb{P}^{n,\alpha}$ let $A(\mathscr{G})$ denote the set of all variables in $\mathscr{G}$ that are improper or not $\mathfrak{i}$-excellent, for $\mathfrak{i}\in\set{0,1}$. For any $v\in V$, and for all $100R \le s \le n^{1/10}$, 
