\begin{proof} Fix a tree $T'\in\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathfrak{c},s}$, as well as a subset $B'\subseteq V_{T'}$ with $|B'| \ge |V_{T'}|/(80R)$ such that all variables in $B'$ lie at pairwise distance greater than $2R$. We consider the event
	\[
	E_n(T',B')
	\equiv\bigg\{\hspace{-3pt}\begin{array}{c}
	\textup{there exists an embedding
	$\zeta:T'\hookrightarrow\mathscr{G}$ such that}\\
	\textup{$\zeta(B')\subseteq A(\mathscr{G})$ and
		$\zeta(T') \cup B_R( \zeta(B');\mathscr{G})$ is acyclic}
	\end{array}\hspace{-3pt}
	\bigg\}\,.
	\]
Write $P_n(T',B') \equiv \mathbb{P}(E_n(T',B'))$
and $P_{n,m}(T',B') \equiv \mathbb{P}_{n,m}(E_n(T',B'))$. Recalling \eqref{e:poisson.erdos.renyi}, we can bound
	\[P_n(T',B')
	\le\sum_{m\ge1} \mathbf{1}\bigg\{
		\frac{|m-n\alpha|}{n^{1/2}\ln n} \le1 \bigg\}
		P_{n,m}(T',B')
