--- the last term accounts for the probability under $\mathbb{P}^{n,\alpha}$ that the total number of clauses in $\mathscr{G}$ (a $\textup{\textsf{Pois}}(n\alpha)$ random variable) deviates from $n\alpha$ by more than $n^{1/2}\ln n$.
