Let $\zeta'$ denote any mapping that sends $V_{T'} \hookrightarrow [n]$, with $\zeta'(v_\textup{\textsc{rt}})=v$, and $F_{T'} \hookrightarrow [m]$; and let $\bm{j}$ denote a mapping $E_{T'} \to [k]$. We then write $\set{\zeta' : T' \hookrightarrow_{\bm{j}} \mathscr{G}}$ for the event that the pair $(\zeta',\bm{j})$ is consistent with an actual embedding of $T'$ into $\mathscr{G}$: this means that for every edge $e=(av)\in E_{T'}$, the edge $\zeta'(e)\equiv (\zeta'(a)\zeta'(v))$ is present in $E_{\mathscr{G}}$, and the index of this edge in the clause $\zeta'(a)$ is given by $\bm{j}(e) \in[k]$. With this notation we can bound
	\begin{equation}\label{e:condition.on.number.of.clauses}
	P_{n,m}(T',B')
