\label{l:prob.Ka.given.Ea}
Let $\mathbb{P}=\mathbb{P}_{n,m}$ for $|m-n\alpha| \le n^{1/2}\ln n$, and $\mathscr{G}\sim\mathbb{P}$. Then, for all $n$ large enough, we have
	\[
	\mathbb{P}\Big(\bm{K}_a(\bm{L}) \,\Big|\,\mathscr{G}\in\bm{E}_a(\bm{L})\Big) 
	\ge \frac{7}{8}\,.
	\]
for all $a\in[m]$ and all clause total types $\bm{L}$ that are feasible in the sense of Definition~\ref{d:feasible.clause.type}.

\begin{proof} Again, throughout the proof $\bm{L}$ is fixed and often suppressed from the notation. Let $\mathscr{G}\sim\mathbb{P}=\mathbb{P}_{n,m}$. Recalling Definition~\ref{d:pos.frac.events}, let $\bm{C}_a$ be the event that there is an embedding $\phi:\mathscr{T}(\bm{L})\hookrightarrow\mathscr{G}$ satisfying properties \eqref{Ea.i}~and~\eqref{Ea.ii} of Definition~\ref{d:pos.frac.events}. Then $\bm{E}_a$ is $\bm{C}_a$ with the additional restriction that $B_{4R}(a;\mathscr{G})$ is a tree. Provided that $\mathscr{G}\in\bm{C}_a$, we define, as in \eqref{e:Gprime.cavity},
	\[\mathscr{G}'\equiv \mathscr{G} \,\bigg\backslash\,
		\phi\Big( \mathscr{T}_\textup{in} \setminus Y\Big)\,.\]
Recalling Definition~\ref{d:pos.frac.events}, we can express $\bm{K}_a$ as the intersection of $\bm{E}_a$ with the event that no variable in $\phi(Y)$ lies within distance $R$ of any variable removed in the processing of $\mathscr{G}'$, equivalently,
	\begin{equation}\label{e:equiv.defn.Ka}
	\bm{K}_a
	= \bm{E}_a\cap \bigg\{
	\textup{$\phi(Y)$ does not intersect
		$S(\mathscr{G}')\equiv B_R\Big(\textup{\textsf{BSP}}'(A';\mathscr{G}');\mathscr{G}'\Big)$}
	\bigg\}\,.
	\end{equation}
Now consider the graph $\mathscr{G}'$ where only $\phi(\mathscr{T}_\textup{out})$ is labelled (in particular, we ignore $\phi(Y)$ for the moment). Let $n'$ denote $n$ minus the number of internal variables in $\mathscr{T}_\textup{in}\setminus Y$. Likewise, let $m'$ denote $m$ minus the number of clauses in $\mathscr{T}_\textup{in}\setminus Y$. Under the measure $\mathbb{P}_{n,m}(\cdot\,|\,\mathscr{G}\in\bm{C}_a)$, the induced law of $\mathscr{G}'$ is equivalent (up to graph isomorphism) to the law $\mathbb{P}_{n',m'}(\cdot\,|\,\mathscr{G}'\in\bm{C}')$ where $\bm{C}'$ is the event that there is an (arbitrary, fixed) embedding $\phi_\textup{out}:\mathscr{T}_\textup{out}\hookrightarrow\mathscr{G}'$. This is only a minor modification of the original measure $\mathbb{P}_{n,m}$, and a trivial extension of Proposition~\ref{p:small.fraction.removed.in.processing} gives
	\begin{equation}\label{e:small.removal.without.girth.cond}
	\mathbb{P}_{n',m'}\bigg(|S(\mathscr{G}')| \ge \frac{n'}{\exp(2^{ck}R)}
	\,\bigg|\,\mathscr{G}'\in \bm{C}'\bigg) = o_n(1)\,.\end{equation}
Since we can choose a fixed embedding $\phi_\textup{out}$, we will suppose that it maps the variables in $\mathscr{T}_\textup{out}$ to the last variables in $\mathscr{G}'$, so that the variables left in $\mathscr{G}'\setminus\phi_\textup{out}(\mathscr{T}_\textup{out})$ can be written as $[n'']=\set{1,\ldots,n''}$. We now return to $Y'\equiv\phi(Y)$, which we regard as an element of
\[
	[n'']_y
	=\Big\{(v_1,\ldots,v_y)\in[n'']^y
	: \textup{$v_i \ne v_j$ for all $i\ne j$}\Big\}\,,
	\]
where $y\equiv|Y|$. Given $(\mathscr{G}',Y')$ where $\mathscr{G}'\in\bm{C}'$ and $Y'\in[n'']_y$, we can uniquely recover the original graph $\mathscr{G}$ (modulo isomorphism) by gluing back the tree $\phi(\mathscr{T}_\textup{in})$, so we write $\mathscr{G}=\mathscr{G}(\mathscr{G}',Y')$ (in this graph, $\phi(\mathscr{T}(\bm{L}))$ is labelled). We then denote
	\begin{equation}\label{e:with.local.girth.cond}
	\bm{J}
	\equiv\bigg\{(\mathscr{G}',Y') \in \bm{C}' \times [n'']_y
	: \textup{in $\mathscr{G}=\mathscr{G}(\mathscr{G}',Y')$,
		the neighborhood $B_{4R}(a;\mathscr{G})$ is a tree}
	\bigg\}\,.
	\end{equation}
Recall from above that under $\mathbb{P}_{n,m}(\cdot\,|\,\mathscr{G}\in\bm{C}_a)$, the induced law of $\mathscr{G}'$ is equivalent (modulo graph isomorphism) to $\mathbb{P}_{n',m'}(\cdot\,|\,\mathscr{G}'\in\bm{C}')$. Recall also that $\bm{E}_a$ is the same as $\bm{C}_a$ with the added restriction that $B_{4R}(a;\mathscr{G})$ is a tree. It follows that if $\bm{K}$ is any event that is invariant under graph isomorphism, then we have
	\begin{equation}\label{e:sample.cavity.graph.up.to.isom}
	\mathbb{P}\Big( (\mathscr{G}',Y')\in\bm{K} \,\Big|\, \mathscr{G}\in \bm{E}_a
	\Big)
	=\mathbb{P}_{n',m'}\Big( (\mathscr{G}',Y')\in\bm{K} \,\Big|\,\bm{J} \Big)\,.\end{equation}
Conditional on $\bm{C}'$, it is clear that $Y'$ is a uniformly random element of $[n'']_y$, which is independent of the structure of $\mathscr{G}'$, and hence independent of $S(\mathscr{G}')$: for any $Y_0\in[n'']_y$ and any subset $S_0\subseteq[n']$,
	\[
	\mathbb{P}_{n',m'}\Big( Y'=Y_0 \,\Big|\,\mathscr{G}'\in\bm{C}', S(\mathscr{G}')=S_0\Big)
	= \frac1{(n'')_y}\,.
	\]
We now argue that this does not change much if we condition further on $B_{4R}(a;\mathscr{G})$ being a tree. Indeed, since all the random graphs we consider are locally tree-like, it is clear that the event $\bm{J}$ of \eqref{e:with.local.girth.cond} occupies $1-o_n(1)$ fraction of $\bm{C}' \times [n'']_y$. This implies that, for any $Y_0\in[n'']_y$ and any $S_0\subseteq[n']$, we have
	\begin{align}\nonumber
	p(Y_0|S_0)
	&\equiv \mathbb{P}_{n',m'}\Big( Y'=Y_0 \,\Big|\, \bm{J}, S(\mathscr{G}')=S_0\Big)
	=\frac{\mathbb{P}_{n',m'}( Y'=Y_0,\bm{J} \,|\, \mathscr{G}'\in\bm{C}',
		 S(\mathscr{G}')=S_0)}
		 {\mathbb{P}_{n',m'}( \bm{J} \,|\, \mathscr{G}'\in\bm{C}',
		 S(\mathscr{G}')=S_0)}\\
	&\le \frac{\mathbb{P}_{n',m'}( Y'=Y_0\,|\, \mathscr{G}'\in\bm{C}',
		 S(\mathscr{G}')=S_0)}
		 {1-o_n(1)}
	= \frac{1-o_n(1)}{(n'')_y}\,.\label{e:exchangeability.Y}
	\end{align}
By a very similar argument, we can extend \eqref{e:small.removal.without.girth.cond} to
	\begin{equation}\label{e:small.removal.with.girth.cond}
