\label{l:matching.of.edges.near.defects}
As in Remark~\ref{r:sample.planted.msr}, 
fix $V,F,\delta V, \delta F$ labelled with total types according to $\mathcal{D}$. From the notion of compound type (Definition~\ref{d:cpd.type}),
for each half-edge $e\in \delta V\sqcup \delta F$, we can deduce from its type $\bm{t}_e$ whether, in the final graph $\mathscr{G}$, the half-edge $e$ will participate in an edge that is internal to a defect. For any matching
$\mathfrak{m}$ of these half-edges, we have $\mathbb{Q}_\mathcal{D}(\mathfrak{m}\subseteq\mathscr{G})=\mathbb{P}_\mathcal{D}(\mathfrak{m}\subseteq\mathscr{G})$.

\begin{proof} As in the statement of the lemma, fix $V,F,\delta V, \delta F$ labelled with total types according to $\mathcal{D}$. It is clear from Definition~\ref{d:cpd.type}
that for a half-edge $e$, the total type $\bm{t}_e$ encodes whether $e$ will participate in an edge that is internal to a defect. That is to say, there is a set of edge types $\mathfrak{T}$ such that $\bm{t}_e\in\mathfrak{T}$ if and only if $e$ participates in the internal edge of a defect. 

Let $\mathscr{G},\mathscr{G}'$ be any two graphs with neighborhood sequence $\mathcal{D}$. Let $\mathscr{H},\mathscr{H}'$ be the corresponding subgraphs induced by their defects; these are encoded by matchings $\mathfrak{m},\mathfrak{m}'$ as described in the statement of the lemma. The matchings involve precisely the half-edges with total types in $\mathfrak{T}$. 
Since defects are contained in enclosures which are encoded by compound types, it follows that $\mathscr{H}$ and $\mathscr{H}'$ are isomorphic
--- equivalently, that there is an isomorphism $\iota$ which takes $\mathfrak{m}\mapsto\mathfrak{m}'$.
Let $\mathscr{G}$ be any graph in which $\mathfrak{m}$ appears. We can extend $\iota$ to $\mathscr{G}$ by applying the identity map to edges not in $\mathfrak{m}$; then
 $\mathfrak{m}'$ appears in $\iota(\mathscr{G})$. If $\smash{\vec{\sigma}}$ is a valid coloring of $\mathscr{G}$, then a valid coloring of $\iota(\mathscr{G})$ is given by
 $(\smash{\vec{\sigma}}\circ \iota^{-1})_e
