We have a bound on
$\mathbb{E}_{\mathscr{D}}\bm{Z}^2[I_1]=\mathbb{E}_\mathcal{D}\bm{Z}^2[I_1]$
from Corollary~\ref{c:intermediate.overlap}.
It follows from the definition of $\mathbb{Q}_\mathcal{D}$ that
	\[
	r'(\mathcal{D})
	\equiv\frac{\mathbb{E}_\mathcal{D}(\bm{Z}_\textup{sep})'}{\mathbb{E}_\mathcal{D}\bm{Z}_\textup{sep}}
	=\mathbb{Q}_\mathcal{D}\Bigg(
	\Bigg\{
	(\mathscr{G},\smash{\vec{\sigma}}):
	\bigg|
	\bigg\{
	\textup{$\smash{\vec{\sigma}}'$}
	:\frac{|v\in V: x(\smash{\vec{\sigma}})_v=x(\smash{\vec{\sigma}}')_v|}{|V|}
	\in I_2
	\bigg\}
	\bigg| \ge \frac{\exp\{(\ln n)^5\}}{2}
	\Bigg\}\Bigg)\,.\]
Recall that the events of Definition~\ref{d:sep.events} all depend on the choice of $(S,P_S)$. To make this explicit, we now write $\bm{K}[S,P_S]\equiv \bm{K}_S$
and $\bm{T}[S,P_S] \equiv \bm{X}_B \cap \bm{Y}_B \cap \bm{K}_S$. It then follows from Lemma~\ref{l:output.s.with.connections} 
and Corollary~\ref{c:sep.main.bound} that
	\[r'(\mathcal{D})
	\le\sum_{(S,P_S)\in\bm{\Pi}_*(\mathcal{D})}
		\mathbb{Q}_\mathcal{D}(\bm{T}[S,P_S] )
	\le\sum_{(S,P_S)\in\bm{\Pi}_*(\mathcal{D})}
		\frac{\mathbb{P}_\mathcal{D}(\bm{K}[S,P_S] )}
		{2^{k(1-3\epsilon_*) (|S|+|F_S|)} }
		\,.
	\]
We now wish to take expectation over the law $\mathbb{P}=\mathbb{P}_{n',m'}$ of the original graph $\mathscr{G}'=(V',F',E')$, of which $\mathscr{G}=\textup{\textsf{pr}}\mathscr{G}'$ is the processed version. To this end, let $\bm{\Pi}'$ denote the set of all pairs $(S,P_S)$ where
$S\subseteq V$ satisfies \eqref{e:sep.bounds.on.size.of.S}, and
 $P_S$ is a collection of tuples
$(u,j_u,a,j_v,v)$ where $u\ne v$ in $S$,
$a\in F'$, every $v\in S$ appears as the last entry of at least one element of $P_S$, and no clause appears more than once in $P_S$.
Note that if $(S,P_S)\in\bm{\Pi}'$ and
$\mathbb{P}_\mathcal{D}(\bm{K}[S,P_S] )$ is positive, then in fact
$(S,P_S)\in\bm{\Pi}(\mathcal{D})$. Thus, writing $\mathbb{E}$ for expectation under $\mathbb{P}$, we have (by the tower property of conditional expectation)
	\begin{align*}
	\mathbb{E} r'(\mathcal{D})
	&\le
	\sum_{(S,P_S)\in\bm{\Pi}'}
	\mathbb{E}\bigg(
	\Ind{(S,P_S)\in\bm{\Pi}(\mathcal{D})}
	\frac{\mathbb{P}_\mathcal{D}(\mathscr{G} \in \bm{K}[S,P_S] )}
		{2^{k(1-3\epsilon_*) (|S|+|F_S|)} }
	\bigg)
	= \sum_{(S,P_S)\in\bm{\Pi}'}
	\mathbb{E}\bigg(
	\frac{\mathbb{P}_\mathcal{D}(\mathscr{G}\in\bm{K}[S,P_S] )}
		{2^{k(1-3\epsilon_*) (|S|+|F_S|)} }
	\bigg)\\
	&= \sum_{(S,P_S)\in\bm{\Pi}'}
	\frac{ \mathbb{P}( \mathscr{G}\in \bm{K}[S,P_S])}
		{2^{k(1-3\epsilon_*) (|S|+|F_S|)} }
	\le \sum_{(S,P_S)\in\bm{\Pi}'}
	\frac{ \mathbb{P}( \mathscr{G}'\in \bm{K}[S,P_S])}
		{2^{k(1-3\epsilon_*) (|S|+|F_S|)} }
	\,,
	\end{align*}
where the last step uses that if $\bm{K}[S,P_S]$ occurs for the processed graph $\mathscr{G}$,
then it also occurs for the original graph $\mathscr{G}'$.
Taking into account the number of choices for $S$ and $P_S$, as well as the probability for the edges to be present under $\mathbb{P}$, we can bound the above as
	\[
	\mathbb{E} r'(\mathcal{D})
	\le
	o_n(1)
	+
	\sum_s
	\mathbf{1}\Bigg\{
	\frac{(\ln n')^2}{n'}
	\le 
	s \le \frac{k^2}{2^k}
	\Bigg\}
	\binom{n'}{n's}
	\frac1{2^{k(1-4\epsilon_*)n's}}
	\Bigg(
	\sum_{\ell\ge1}
