In the above, the $o_n(1)$ error accounts for the probability that more than $o_R(1)$ fraction of variables are removed during preprocessing, which is controlled by Proposition~\ref{p:small.fraction.removed.in.processing}. On the complementary event, the number of variables $n$ in $\mathscr{G}$ is very close to the original number of variables $n'$, so the restriction on $s=|S|/n'$ follows from \eqref{e:sep.bounds.on.size.of.S}.
The inner sum over $\ell\ge1$ is for the possible sizes of the sets $P(v)$. Simplifying the above gives
