Recall for $j=1,2$ we use $(P_e)^j$ to denote the marginal of $P_e$ on the $j$-th copy. Then
	\begin{align*}
	\mathcal{X}(\SPIN{Y}\SPIN{W})
	&=\prod_{e\in\delta a \setminus e'}
		\Bigg\{ (P_e)^1(\SSPIN{y})
		- P_e(\SSPIN{y}\SSPIN{r})\Bigg\}
	= \prod_{e\in\delta a \setminus e'}
		\Bigg\{ (Q_e)^1(\SSPIN{y})
			\Big( 1 + O({}^\textup{m}\hspace{-2pt}\delta_e)\Big)
		- Q_e(\SSPIN{y}\SSPIN{r})
