	= z_\star\nu_\star(\SPIN{+}\SPIN{+})
	\Bigg\{ 1 + O\bigg(\frac{k^{O(1)}}{2^{k\zeta}}
	\bigg)\Bigg\}\,,
	\end{align*}
and the same estimate holds for the other spins in $\set{\SPIN{+}\SPIN{-},\SPIN{-}\SPIN{+},\SPIN{-}\SPIN{-}}$. Therefore
	\begin{equation}\label{e:frozen.product.approx.pi}
