(depending only on $\epsilon_2$) such that for every edge $e\in\delta v(x)$ we have
	\[\left.
	\begin{array}{r}
	\bm{\varpi}_{\bm{L},j}( 
		\upsilon=\SPIN{v}\SPIN{v} \,|\, \sigma=\SSPIN{r}\SSPIN{r})\\
	\bm{\varpi}_{\bm{L},j}( \upsilon^1=\SPIN{v}
		\,|\, \sigma=\SSPIN{r}\SSPIN{b} )\\
	\bm{\varpi}_{\bm{L},j}(
		\upsilon^2=\SPIN{v} \,|\,\sigma=\SSPIN{b}\SSPIN{r} )\\
	\end{array} \hspace{-4pt}
